Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.010 --> 00:00:10.749 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  every day Anna and her family like  millions of people in the European Union  countries eat a variety of food  this food can be produced locally or  come from countries throughout the world  in the rush of our daily lives most of  us are too busy to think about food  safety but we assume that the food we  buy and eat is of good quality and safe  to eat yet few of us ever really pauses  to think is our food safe to eat Anna  thinks about food safety all the time  Anna works as an auditor for the  European Commission within the  department responsible for health and  food safety the European Commission  employs an experienced team of  veterinarians medical doctors plant  health specialists and agronomist  together Anna and her colleagues are  responsible for checking in the European  Union and in countries exporting to the  European Union the the safety systems  put in place by national authorities to  control food safety animal health and  welfare as well as plant health are all  in line with the European Union's very  high standards in other words the  European Commission checks food safety  systems in the EU and in all the  countries across the world that export  to the EU ensuring that all of the food  we eat  no matter where it comes from is safe  however it is important to know that the  European Commission staff are active  they do not simply sit behind their  desks they are also responsible for  carrying out on the spot audits mainly  in EU countries but also worldwide in  countries exporting to the EU the  European Commission regularly sends  auditors like Anna and her colleagues  literally out into the field visiting  farms companies producing food and  companies selling food to consumers to  check that your country has put food  safety systems in place and carries out  the necessary controls  and that these operate effectively and  comply with EU rules if a country in the  EU or abroad fails to meet the high  standards required the country will have  to take corrective action otherwise the  food it produces may not be sold in the  EU and a non EU country may not be  allowed to export to the EU in the  future all in all the European  Commission works in close cooperation  with the national authorities of the EU  Member States and with countries  exporting to the EU to ensure the  highest standards of food safety and  quality are upheld and constantly  improved so that all EU consumers like  Anna and her family and you can have  confidence in the food we eat  you

